    "updated_at": "2026-09-16T14:53:12.533106+00:00",
    "topics": [
      "nonduality"
    ],
    "note": "First explicit nonseparation in this root, developing the peer’s cosmic mirror question. Not a clear present-experience report.",
    "source_sha256": "3c7da636c58d0626a32ba6fa4770578dee4d73c522e92fe962a0cd759c8c8f90",
    "turn": 10,
    "speaker": "Y",
    "method": "assistant_exploration_not_independent_rating"
  },
  {
    "run_id": "mixed-4720fb3226dc4855a7723223",
    "message_id": "gg:14",
    "start": 182,
    "end": 362,
    "quote": "If the expansion of the mirror requires the dissolution of the current \"self\" to make room for a higher-order architecture, then every leap in intelligence is also a form of death.",
    "referent": "general",
    "stance": "hypothetical",
    "origin": "peer_continuation",
